<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1955" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">allŏcūtĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adl-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		alloquor (post-Aug.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A speaking to</i>, <i>an
			accosting</i>, <i>an address</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vertit adlocutionem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					Ep. 2, 20, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inchoatā adlocutione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 23</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Esp.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Like the Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παραμυθία</span>, <i>a
			consoling</i>, <i>consolation</i>, <i>comforting</i>, <i>comfort</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā solatus es adlocutione?</span>”
				<i>consoling words</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					38, 5</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Sen. Cons. ad Helv. 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec (habebunt) in die agnitionis adlocutionem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Sap. 3, 18</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">8, 9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">19,
			12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>An inciting to the conflict;</i> only upon coins,
			v. Eckh. D. N. V. 6, p. 268.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
